      "source": "Le bateau viking dOseberg (4836398163)",
      "description": "Oseberg's boat in the Viking Boat Museum in Oslo (Vikingskipshuset).\nThis boat, unearthed in 1904, was built between 815 and 820 and was used as a funeral boat for a high-ranking woman who died in 834. The body was in a wooden funeral chamber placed on the bridge. Around the body have been discovered many objects in wood, leather and textiles.\nThe boat, 22 m long, is made of oak wood. It had 30 rowers and was not a boat built for the high seas.\n\nThe museum presents three Viking boats, very well preserved, as well as objects, which have been discovered in three funerary mounds near Oslo Fjord.",
